Support continuation of Eduten gamified learning platform for grade 5th Math lessons after the piloting with Global Learning Innovation Hub;   				
Support conducting country analysis to formulate concrete challenges and possible digital learning futures within Learning pioneering initiative; 				
Organize a series of workshops and discussions to support designing EdTech solutions and how it could be tested and scaled  in Uzbekistan; 				
Support piloting of selected EdTech solutions in the country;

Upgrading of existing infrastructure of 50 model schools against developed accessibility check lists for school accessibility (e.g. entry, ramps, signage, doors, stairs, toilets, furniture, etc.);				
Establishment of digital labs with assistive technologies in model schools;				
Capacity building and training programmes for school management teams, teachers and multidisciplinary inclusion teams in schools				
Introduction of school inclusive Disaster Risk Management plans;

Strengthen the Government's capacity to understand the importance of child poverty and its implications for child wellbeing, the country’s development and achieving SDGs;
Equip the Government with methods and tools to systematically measure and monitor monetary child poverty;
Equip the Government with methods and tools to systematically measure multidimensional child poverty in line with the international standards to inform policymaking, programs and budgets.

Strengthen the capacity of the Statistics Agency, CERR and MoEPR in the analysis and reporting of the monetary and multidimensional child poverty data and for tracking the progress of implementation of SDGs on poverty.

Support review and gaps analysis of current knowlwdge and practicies of preschool teachers' and managers and development of recommendations and road map for improving in-service training programme;			
Revision of in-service training programme for teachers based on new curriculum and programme for training managers (along with capacity building of MOPSE Working Group /national experts);				
Equipping Regional Cluster Centres for in-service training (Decentralized) by distribution of equipment, training package for preschool teachers on preschool curriculum & ELDS and managers on preschool management;		
Development of the training programme and materials for the training of Master Trainers and Teachers of In-Service teachers training Institute on new Curricula and Training of Master Trainers;

prioritize capacity-building activities of the Ministry of Health of Karakalpakstan, and primary care providers in Non-communicable diseases (NCD) prevention and management programme which includes the followings: 
-building the capacity of nurses in CVD risk stratification based on PEN/HEARTS protocols; 
-building the capacity of nurses to develop community profiles with information on the social determinants of health (SES, employment, housing conditions, isolation)  to inform and expand the basis for CVD risk stratification ; 
-follow-up visits for chronic diseases, advance appointments, queue management, “pre-doctoral” consultations and triage; 
- resolutive capacity of family doctors to optimize referrals to specialists; mobile teams

Support to CED in development of competency-based, inclusive and gender transformative requirements to educational standards;				
Support MOPSE in finalizing CBE National Curriculum Framework;			
Support MOPSE/CED in development of roadmap for implementation of NCF;

Support in development of framework and mechanisms for Inclusive Preschools;	
Pilot of frameworks and mechanisms in 10 preschools;			
Design of the Behavior Change Strategy and roll out of the campaign;

Developing Learning assessment framework and associated legislation;  				
Methodological support and capacity building for introduction of classroom assessment; 				
